#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute Code Runtimes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "execute_code Multi-Runtime"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "> One tool, multiple runtimes; default Bun; extend with Python / Deno as needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:12
msgid ""
"`execute_code` runs short scripts in a controlled subprocess. The LLM must "
"know which language to write and which runtime to pick — otherwise Python "
"sent to Node fails."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Division from terminal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|           | `execute_code`                               | `terminal`                                                               |\n"
"| --------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| Execution | No shell, fixed runtime                      | Default `shell=false` (argv); `shell=true` for pipes/redirection         |\n"
"| Best for  | Short scripts, data processing, logic checks | System commands, git, long tasks; pipes need `shell=true`                |\n"
"| Output    | 50KB cap, configurable timeout               | Same limits                                                              |\n"
"| Security  | No shell injection; **not** a FS sandbox     | Catastrophic command hard deny + workdir path policy; still ≠ OS sandbox |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:23
msgid ""
"Use `execute_code(runtime=\"python\")` for Python batches, not `python3 -c "
"\"...\"` in terminal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (typescript)
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"execute_code({\n"
"  code: string,\n"
"  runtime?: \"bun\" | \"nodejs\" | \"python\" | \"deno\",  // default bun\n"
"  timeout?: number,       // seconds, default 300, max 600\n"
"})\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "Available Runtimes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| runtime    | Language                | Status                  |\n"
"| ---------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------- |\n"
"| **bun**    | TypeScript / JavaScript | ✅ default              |\n"
"| **nodejs** | TypeScript / JavaScript | ✅ implemented          |\n"
"| **python** | Python                  | 🔲 reserved (Issue #40) |\n"
"| **deno**   | TypeScript              | 🔲 reserved (Issue #40) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration (Reserved)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"execute_code:\n"
"  default_runtime: bun\n"
"  runtimes:\n"
"    nodejs:\n"
"      enabled: true\n"
"    python:\n"
"      enabled: true\n"
"      command: python3\n"
"    deno:\n"
"      enabled: false\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:59
msgid "Disabled runtimes return a clear error listing available runtimes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:66
msgid "Always `shell: false` (see [`security.md`](../guide/security.md))"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:66
msgid "Timeout and output size limits match current implementation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:66
msgid "**Do not** auto-guess runtime from code content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:66
msgid ""
"JS runtimes can still import `node:fs`—terminal command hard denies do "
"**not** apply inside `code_execute`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "Credential Injection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:70
msgid ""
"`code_execute` (and `terminal_run`) accept optional `secrets[]`: Vault item "
"refs decrypted for **that subprocess only** and merged into child `env` (not "
"Habitat `process.env`). Values never appear in LLM tool results. Prefer "
"argv / `process.env.NAME` inside the snippet; no vault CLI inside runtimes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code.md:71
msgid ""
"File-path credential mounts (Issue #40 style) are **not** implemented; use "
"`secrets[]` for CLI/runtime needs."
msgstr ""
